cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, the certificates, or the Lean formalisation, please cite
  this repository. For the mathematics, cite the manuscript the result belongs
  to: the odd-degree note (preferred citation below) or the even-degree
  companion (listed under references).
title: >-
  The Hodge conjecture for Fermat fourfolds: odd degrees at most 199 and the
  even-degree census through 250 — papers, code, certificates, and Lean
  formalisation
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jumagulov
    given-names: Rifat
    email: jum.rifm@gmail.com
version: 1.0.4
date-released: "2026-07-29"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rifmj/fermat-fourfolds-boundary"
keywords:
  - Hodge conjecture
  - Fermat fourfolds
  - algebraic cycles
  - Hodge classes
  - Aoki lattice
  - Jacobi sums
  - exact arithmetic
  - computer-assisted proof
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  Two companion manuscripts and the single self-verifying computational package
  they share. The odd-degree note proves the Hodge conjecture for the Fermat
  fourfold of every odd degree at most 199, and rules out a field of definition
  inside the 33rd cyclotomic field for the exceptional block by an exact
  Jacobi-sum computation at p = 67. The even-degree companion maps the even
  sector through degree 250: forty primitive classes survive the base predicates
  and the depth-2 closure oracle, deeper certificates close all but ten, an
  exchange theorem organises the residual into claim-equivalence walls, and two
  walls close, leaving eight certified gap classes, which are not claimed to be
  non-algebraic. The package carries three independent census implementations,
  per-orbit witnesses for all 78,299 orbit representatives, canonical per-level
  hashes, exact lattice certificates, explicit routes for all thirty deep
  closures, and verifiers each tested to reject a corrupted certificate.
